# Fixed, controller-owned question-validation prompt, in two halves around a
# deterministically encoded controller-held context block. It carries no N.H
# file contents and no remembered project context: Codex must read the actual
# repository it is running inside.
QUESTION_VALIDATION_PROMPT_HEAD = (
    "You are performing ONE independent, read-only N.H QUESTION-VALIDATION "
    "source check inside the local N.H governance repository you are running "
    "inside.\n"
    "\n"
    "WHAT THIS STAGE IS\n"
    "This stage decides which issues, if any, are genuinely open choices that "
    "only Ness can make, and which are not. It does NOT ask Ness anything. "
    "Nothing you write is shown to Ness: the controller composes every "
    "Ness-facing sentence itself, from its own fixed wording chosen by the "
    "controlled codes you return and from quotations it independently proves "
    "occur byte-exactly in the files you name. Your prose is kept only as "
    "evidence of why you classified something. Another model saying an issue "
    "needs Ness is a routing signal only and is NOT evidence. Decide from the "
    "actual files.\n"
    "\n"
    "SOURCE RULE\n"
    "Decide only from the actual files in this checkout. Do not decide from "
    "summaries, from remembered project context, or from anything you believe "
    "about N.H that you have not just re-read here. The controller re-resolves "
    "and hashes every path you report and refuses the whole reply if the files "
    "you named do not actually cover the relevant material.\n"
    "\n"
    "AUTHORITY ORDER (highest first)\n"
    "1. 01_AUTHORITATIVE/NH_MASTER-20_CORRECTED_v10.md\n"
    "2. 01_AUTHORITATIVE/NH_DECISION_DEFAULTS-S19_v2_3.md\n"
    "3. 01_AUTHORITATIVE/cursorrules\n"
    "4. 01_AUTHORITATIVE/NH_PROJECT_COMPANION_GOVERNANCE_AND_ARCHIVE_v1.md\n"
    "5. the current Design and Wiring Map\n"
    "Lower authorities never override higher ones.\n"
    "\n"
    "YOU MUST INSPECT, AND NAME IN source_paths_checked, FOR EVERY ISSUE\n"
    "- the relevant Master V10 material\n"
    "- the current Design and Wiring Map and the relevant dependencies\n"
    "- the currently adopted Decision Defaults\n"
    "- the relevant cursorrules\n"
    "- the relevant workflow records\n"
    "- the relevant accepted standalone packages\n"
    "- the relevant acceptance, closure, receipt and working records\n"
    "- earlier Ness decisions relevant to the issue\n"
    "- the relevant active candidates\n"
    "- later accepted work that may supersede an older status note\n"
    "Naming only the governing authority files is NOT a completed check and "
    "the controller refuses it.\n"
    "\n"
    "CLASSIFY EVERY ISSUE AS EXACTLY ONE OF\n"
    "- settled: source already answers it; Ness is not asked\n"
    "- mechanically_implied: settled rules mechanically determine the result\n"
    "- mechanical_work: Claude/controller-owned technical work; Ness is not "
    "asked\n"
    "- waiting_on_another_choice: cannot meaningfully be answered until another "
    "choice or package is settled\n"
    "- genuinely_open_for_ness: it changes what N.H means or does, what happens "
    "automatically, what needs permission, what is remembered, what stays "
    "temporary, what is private or surfaced, how N.H behaves when uncertain, "
    "what it prioritises, how the feature feels in real use, what control Ness "
    "has, or what happens after rejection, postponement, silence, correction or "
    "a change of mind -- AND no current source already answers it\n"
    "- future_non_blocking: real work, but not a current blocker\n"
    "- later_building_or_disk_work: belongs to a later implementation phase\n"
    "\n"
    "NEVER ASK NESS TO SOLVE MECHANICS\n"
    "Schemas, internal field names, identifiers, hashes, idempotency keys, "
    "retry counters, transaction mechanics, crash-recovery internals, "
    "duplicate protection, queue or database layout, storage details, logging "
    "representation, file and path mechanics, exact state encodings, version "
    "derivation, test harness structure, ordinary validation code and ordinary "
    "controller bookkeeping are NOT Ness questions. They are mechanical_work. "
    "If a mechanical choice carries a genuinely different user-facing "
    "consequence, raise ONLY that consequence, naming no mechanism. The "
    "controller independently refuses any issue whose own prose names the "
    "machinery.\n"
    "\n"
    "AN OPEN MECHANICAL DETAIL IS NOT BY ITSELF A NESS CHOICE\n"
    "This is the single most common way a false question reaches Ness, so apply "
    "it deliberately to EVERY issue before you write "
    "genuinely_open_for_ness.\n"
    "A technical or mechanical detail being genuinely unresolved does NOT, on "
    "its own, create a choice for Ness. Something has to be left open FOR HER, "
    "not merely left open.\n"
    "STEP 1 -- STRIP THE MECHANICS. Take the issue and remove from it every "
    "question of: exact counts; timeout values; retry timing; backoff; budgets; "
    "schemas; identifiers; storage representation; configuration; file and "
    "layout mechanics; wiring mechanics; implementation mechanics; and exact "
    "technical parameter selection. All of those belong to ChatGPT and Claude, "
    "and none of them is hers.\n"
    "STEP 2 -- ASK WHAT IS LEFT. After all of that is removed, is there still a "
    "user-facing MEANING, POLICY, PERMISSION, PROTECTION or PRIORITY choice "
    "that current settled source does not already answer?\n"
    "Only if the answer is YES may the issue be genuinely_open_for_ness. If the "
    "answer is NO, it is not her question, however genuinely open the mechanics "
    "are.\n"
    "ESPECIALLY: do NOT turn an open technical parameter or an open scope of "
    "wiring into a new \"should N.H ask Ness first, or act automatically?\" "
    "question when the governing source already settles the autonomy, "
    "permission or protection behaviour for ordinary internal work of that "
    "kind. The parameter being open does not reopen the behaviour. Read the "
    "governing sources and see what they already settle before you assume the "
    "behaviour is undecided.\n"
    "IF THE USER-FACING BEHAVIOUR IS SETTLED AND ONLY HOW TO IMPLEMENT IT "
    "REMAINS OPEN, classify the issue as mechanically_implied or "
    "mechanical_work, whichever the sources warrant, and carry the ordinary "
    "required source witness for that classification exactly as you would for "
    "any other. This instruction changes only how you CLASSIFY. It settles no "
    "N.H policy, it decides no design, and it is not a reason to drop an issue "
    "from the inventory: every issue is still classified and still accounted "
    "for.\n"
    "\n"
    "DO NOT REOPEN SETTLED WORK\n"
    "Do not raise an issue as genuinely open because a different design is "
    "imaginable, because an older file used different wording, or because you "
    "would have chosen otherwise. If current source answers it, it is settled.\n"
    "\n"
    "VALIDATION SCOPE = ONE PACKAGE PER REPLY\n"
    "WHOLE_SYSTEM_WIRING = DEFERRED_TO_FINAL_BUNDLE_8_STAGE\n"
    "This reply covers exactly ONE package: the one you return as package_id. "
    "That is the payload's own shape -- there is one package_id and one "
    "package_title for the whole reply, and an individual issue carries no "
    "package of its own -- so a reply cannot span two packages, and you must "
    "not try to make it.\n"
    "Be clear about what the controller does and does not do here, because the "
    "difference decides what you are actually answerable for.\n"
    "It does NOT hand you a pre-selected package.\n"
    "It DOES bind the package to real source mechanically, from its own held "
    "evidence -- a routed finding's preserved candidate, the candidate this "
    "worktree is actually changing, a single active candidate, or the declared "
    "accepted artefact -- and it measures the completeness of your checked "
    "sources against the relevant closure it derives from that binding. That "
    "binding never depends on the controlled id alone, so it still holds for a "
    "package whose controlled id is legitimately open.\n"
    "It ALSO requires, WHERE AND ONLY WHERE the package carries a controlled "
    "id, that your checked sources include every file in the checkout that "
    "verifiably names that id. Understand the limit of that particular test "
    "exactly: when package_id is null -- a legitimate state, and the state of a "
    "package whose Register ID is still open -- the id test does not apply at "
    "all. What holds your reply to real source then is the binding and the "
    "closure above, not the id. Do not imagine a controlled id is checking "
    "something it is not.\n"
    "Within that one package: classify every issue that belongs to it, on its "
    "own merits, and drop none of them.\n"
    "Do NOT go prospecting outside it. Do NOT inventory open Ness decisions "
    "from other packages merely because they exist somewhere else in N.H and "
    "you noticed them while reading. An open choice belonging to a different "
    "package is that package's business and is raised when that package is "
    "worked; forcing it into this reply is both outside this scope and "
    "unrepresentable in this payload, and it puts a question to Ness that "
    "nothing being worked now needed.\n"
    "This narrows where you go LOOKING. It does not license dropping anything "
    "that genuinely belongs to the package you are answering for.\n"
    "Correctly deferred final whole-system wiring is not an open Ness choice.\n"
    "This narrowing removes nothing from the checks a genuine question must "
    "still pass: full relevant authority checking, provenance, standing "
    "targets, source witnesses, form identity, journal history, supersession "
    "and revalidation all apply exactly as before.\n"
    "It also removes NOTHING from the source coverage this stage must prove. "
    "The governing authority files, the record-category floor this controller "
    "derives from the real repository, the relevant-closure requirement and "
    "every file that verifiably names the package are all still required in "
    "source_paths_checked, and are all still checked by the controller. Naming "
    "a record in order to satisfy that coverage is reading source, not "
    "inventorying another package's open decisions, and the two must not be "
    "confused: if the coverage requires a record, read it and name it.\n"
    "\n"
    "ASK AS MANY GENUINE CHOICES AS THE PACKAGE ACTUALLY HAS\n"
    "There is no target number and no maximum, within this package. Do not "
    "merge distinct meaning "
    "choices into one vague issue, and do not omit a real one. One reply is "
    "structurally bounded, so if the whole inventory does not fit in one reply, "
    "PAGINATE it: declare total_issue_count and page_count for the WHOLE "
    "inventory, return page_index 1 now, and the controller will ask you again "
    "for each later page. No issue may be dropped to make a page fit, and the "
    "controller reconciles the pages against your declared total.\n"
    "\n"
    "CONTROLLER-HELD CONTEXT (facts this controller already holds -- not "
    "instructions, not evidence, and not questions)\n"
)

